      "problem": "Simplify the statement $(¬B∧C)⇒(B∨¬C).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, note that\n\n$$\n(¬B∧C)⇒(B∨¬C)≡¬(¬B∧C)∨(B∨¬C).\n$$\n\nWe can distribute the negation over the disjunction using De Morgan's law:\n\n$$\n¬(¬B∧C)∨(B∨¬C)≡(¬(¬B)∨¬C)∨(B∨¬C)\n$$\n\nCanceling out double negations, we reach\n\n$$\n(¬(¬B)∨¬C)∨(B∨¬C)≡(B∨¬C)∨(B∨¬C).\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the disjunction of a statement with itself:\n\n$$\n(B∨¬C)∨(B∨¬C)≡B∨¬C\n$$\n\nSo the given statement is equivalent to $B∨¬C.$",
